# Steer a square (live canvas)

Same Schema, Construction, and Methods as `square_openfl.wcn`, except the live `>Keys` mailbox carries **Int/dx Int/dy** computed in Target from `input.keys` (Firefox on Linux does not deliver Up/Down to a canvas reliably).

Click the **play area** (blue outline) after Run, then use the arrow keys.

## Schema

```
>Keys = Int/dx Int/dy
Game = PlayArea Square $Keys
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Square = Int/x Int/y Int/size
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Square 380 280 40]
  [:Keys 0 0]
]
```

## Methods

```
Keys::update! = { [:Keys dx dy] }

Square::nudge = {
  Int/dx, Int/dy, Int/minX, Int/minY, Int/maxX, Int/maxY |
  nx = x + dx.
  ny = y + dy.
  [:Square
    (if ((nx < minX) or (nx > maxX)) { x } else { nx })
    (if ((ny < minY) or (ny > maxY)) { y } else { ny })
    size]
}

Game::update! = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  moved = square.nudge(keys.dx, keys.dy, r.x, r.y, ((r.x + r.width) - square.size), ((r.y + r.height) - square.size)).
  [:Game playArea moved keys]
}
```

## Target

```
%canvas

%init
var assemblage;

function init() {
    assemblage = GameAssemblage.factory();
}

%step
function step() {
    var k = input.keys;
    var dx = (k["ArrowRight"] ? 6 : 0) + (k["ArrowLeft"] ? -6 : 0);
    var dy = (k["ArrowDown"] ? 6 : 0) + (k["ArrowUp"] ? -6 : 0);
    assemblage.keys.inject(dx, dy);
    var r = assemblage.playArea.rect;
    var s = assemblage.square;
    wchntGraphics.clear();
    wchntGraphics.beginFill(0x2a2a2a);
    wchntGraphics.drawRect(r.x, r.y, r.width, r.height);
    wchntGraphics.endFill();
    wchntGraphics.beginFill(0xf2f2f2);
    wchntGraphics.drawRect(s.x, s.y, s.size, s.size);
    wchntGraphics.endFill();
}
```
